    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\nAcura to Launch Three New SUVs in the U.S., Including Its Largest Ever With Eight Seats\n15 photos\nPhoto: Acura\nFollowing a period of trouble one or two years ago, the automotive industry, at least the one over in America, seems to be on a rebound. And there’s no better indication of that than the rising sales in the luxury segment.\nTake Japanese Acura , for instance. In the first nine months of the year, the Honda offshoot brags about growing faster than several established luxury competitors that it does not name. Compared to the same period of last year, it sold 4.4 percent more cars.\nThe growth was driven, in part, by one of its models, the MDX, which not only managed to hold on to the title of best-selling three-row luxury SUV of all time, but also increased its sales by a staggering 25 percent.\nOn top of that, the carmaker’s ADX and Integra models lead the sales charts in their respective segments, with just three months left in the year.\nAll of the above seems to have seeded into the heads of the company’s execs the idea that there is more room to grow on the market for Acura. And this week, that idea materialized into a new product plan for the near future.\nAs you know, at the time of writing, the company sells just four models on the American market, namely the Integra sport sedan and the three SUVs, namely the ADX, RDX, and MDX. These will be joined in the coming years by three more SUVs, including the largest the Japanese have ever made, targeting segments it hasn’t played in so far.\nTwo of these machines will land in 2028. The first is a new adventure-ready vehicle that will bring a luxury touch to off-roading activities, something more and more people seem to be into these days. No details about it have been released so far.\nThe second SUV will be the next, fourth generation of the RDX, but we already knew about that. The SUV will, however, become the company’s first product to be fitted with a two-motor hybrid drivetrain.\nThe star of the announcement is, however, the new eight-passenger SUV that will hit the market later down the line. We’re told this vehicle will become the largest one Acura has ever made, fitting right above the seven-passenger MDX, and will directly target families in need of roomier rides, among others.\nOn top of the three SUVs, Acura also announced it is working on a new hybrid V6 powertrain, aimed to fit under the hood of the RDX above all. No details about it have been revealed so far, but we expect that to change soon.\nWe will keep an eye on Acura and its dealings in the U.S. market and report back once we know more about that.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nEditor's note: Gallery shows the 2025 Acura MDX.\nAcura Acura MDX Acura RDX\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Daniel Patrascu\nDaniel loves writing (or so he claims), and he uses this skill to offer readers a \"behind the scenes\" look at the automotive industry. He also enjoys talking about space exploration and robots, because in his view the only way forward for humanity is away from this planet, in metal bodies. Full profile\nUP NEXT 2027 Honda Civic Sedan and Hatchback Arrive in the US, New Sport-L Trim Will Start Below $28,500",
